{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q4454243","formula":"SnTe","hill":"SnTe","elements":["Sn","Te"],"composition":{"Sn":1.0,"Te":1.0},"names":{"en":"Tin telluride","ru":"Теллурид олова"},"descriptions":{"en":"Tin telluride is a compound of tin and tellurium (SnTe); is a IV-VI narrow band gap semiconductor and has direct band gap of 0.18 eV. It is often alloyed with lead to make lead tin telluride, which is used as an infrared detector material. Tin telluride normally forms p-type semiconductor (Extrinsic semiconductor) due to tin vacancies and is a low temperature superconductor. SnTe exists in three crystal phases.","ru":"Теллурид олова — полупроводник, представляет собой соединение олова и теллура (SnTe). Имеет широкую одностороннюю область гомогенности, высокую концентрацию собственных дефектов (катионных вакансий) и носителей заряда p-типа (~ 1020—1021 см−3)."},"fame":14,"pubchemCid":6432000,"mass":246.3,"charge":0,"smiles":"[Sn]=[Te]","inchikey":"WYUZTTNXJUJWQQ-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"tellanylidenetin","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-1883","atoms":27,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[6.372,0.0,0.0],[0.0,6.372,0.0],[0.0,0.0,6.372]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"Sn"},{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":6.372,"el":"Sn"},{"x":0.0,"y":6.372,"z":0.0,"el":"Sn"},{"x":0.0,"y":6.372,"z":6.372,"el":"Sn"},{"x":6.372,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"Sn"},{"x":6.372,"y":0.0,"z":6.372,"el":"Sn"},{"x":6.372,"y":6.372,"z":0.0,"el":"Sn"},{"x":6.372,"y":6.372,"z":6.372,"el":"Sn"},{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":3.186,"el":"Te"},{"x":0.0,"y":6.372,"z":3.186,"el":"Te"},{"x":6.372,"y":0.0,"z":3.186,"el":"Te"},{"x":6.372,"y":6.372,"z":3.186,"el":"Te"},{"x":0.0,"y":3.186,"z":3.186,"el":"Sn"},{"x":6.372,"y":3.186,"z":3.186,"el":"Sn"},{"x":0.0,"y":3.186,"z":0.0,"el":"Te"},{"x":0.0,"y":3.186,"z":6.37